 "case:locations.archive.description": "The archive is colder than the rest of the building. Shelves of old programme tapes line one wall; contracts and royalty ledgers fill another. A staff-only door at the back opens onto the narrow passage behind the studios.",
 "case:locations.archive.hotspots.hs_archive_contract.label": "The Clearwater file",
 "case:locations.archive.hotspots.hs_archive_contract.text": "The Clearwater file is missing from its box. A photocopy remains underneath: a two-page agreement signed by Rookery’s rights department, with a handwritten amendment that directs the payments elsewhere.",
 "case:locations.archive.hotspots.hs_archive_ledger.label": "The rights ledger",
 "case:locations.archive.hotspots.hs_archive_ledger.text": "The current ledger lists the programmes sold to Vesper Media. One line is marked in pencil: Clearwater Rights, 17 percent of every archive licence, payable to a company whose name has been blacked out.",
 "case:locations.archive.hotspots.hs_archive_passage.label": "The staff passage",
 "case:locations.archive.hotspots.hs_archive_passage.text": "The passage is too narrow for two people to pass comfortably. It runs from the archive door to the back of Studio B, behind a layer of acoustic panels. There is no camera here, only a small red door-contact light.",
 "case:locations.archive.hotspots.hs_archive_scans.label": "The document scanner",
 "case:locations.archive.hotspots.hs_archive_scans.text": "The scanner keeps a local activity log. Friday’s last scan was made at 21:41 using Iris Chen’s staff code. After that, the next scan is dated Monday morning, although the archive door was opened again before midnight.",
 "case:locations.archive.name": "The archive",
 "case:locations.archive.summary": "Rookery’s paper contracts, rights ledgers, and the staff passage to Studio B.",
 "case:locations.quay.art.props.0.label": "Rookery Audio",
 "case:locations.quay.art.props.1.label": "River",
 "case:locations.quay.art.props.2.label": "Public entrance",
 "case:locations.quay.art.props.3.label": "Loading yard",
 "case:locations.quay.description": "Rookery Audio sits in a long brick warehouse beside the river. The public entrance faces the quay; a staff door opens onto the loading yard. Inside, reception looks down a central corridor, with the two studios on one side and the archive at the far end.",
 "case:locations.quay.hotspots.hs_quay_door.label": "The staff door",
 "case:locations.quay.hotspots.hs_quay_door.text": "The loading-yard door is shut and alarmed. Its little green light is steady. A smear of river grit lies on the threshold, but the rain has made every footprint outside useless.",
 "case:locations.quay.hotspots.hs_quay_layout.label": "The warehouse plan",
 "case:locations.quay.hotspots.hs_quay_layout.text": "A framed plan beside the entrance labels the public corridor, the two studios, the archive, and a narrow staff passage that runs behind the soundproofing. The archive has its own door onto that passage. Studio B’s only public-facing door is at the opposite end of the corridor.",
 "case:locations.quay.hotspots.hs_quay_sign.label": "The paused announcement",
 "case:locations.quay.hotspots.hs_quay_sign.text": "A printed notice on the glass says the Vesper Media announcement is postponed until further notice. Someone has crossed out ‘midnight’ in black marker, then written it again beneath the line.",
 "case:locations.quay.name": "North Quay",
 "case:locations.quay.summary": "The warehouse entrance, loading yard, and the short route between reception and the studios.",
 "case:locations.reception.art.props.0.label": "Desk",
 "case:locations.reception.art.props.1.label": "Key cabinet",
 "case:locations.reception.art.props.2.label": "Camera monitor",
 "case:locations.reception.art.props.3.label": "Visitor book",
 "case:locations.reception.art.props.4.label": "Corridor",
 "case:locations.reception.description": "The reception desk is made from a flight case painted Rookery blue. Behind it hang the building keys, each on a numbered hook. A small monitor shows the corridor camera in black and white; the camera sees the studio doors but not the archive passage.",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_hotel.label": "Felix’s hotel card",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_hotel.text": "A hotel card lies beneath the visitor book. The front desk at the Brighton Marine confirms a late check-in, but the time has been written in pencil rather than printed by the hotel system.",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_keys.label": "The key cabinet",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_keys.text": "The cabinet has hooks for every room and two heavier keys labelled MASTER A and MASTER B. The sign beneath says that master keys must be returned before leaving the building. One hook is empty; the sign-out sheet is clipped below it.",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_monitor.label": "The corridor monitor",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_monitor.text": "The corridor camera records in short clips whenever the building alarm changes state. The monitor has been left on the clip list for Friday night. The image is grainy, but the timecode is clear enough to read.",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_receipt.label": "The desk drawer",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_receipt.text": "Under old courier labels is a folded taxi receipt, paid by card at 21:12. The passenger name is not printed, but the booking reference is written in Anika Rao’s handwriting on the back.",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_visitors.label": "The visitor book",
 "case:locations.reception.hotspots.hs_reception_visitors.text": "The visitor book is open to Friday. A Vesper Media name is written at 20:04, followed by a neat departure time. The next line is blank, though a second cup has left a damp ring on the paper.",
 "case:locations.reception.name": "Reception",
 "case:locations.reception.summary": "The front desk, key cabinet, visitor book, and the camera looking into the central corridor.",
 "case:locations.studios.art.props.0.label": "Studio A",
 "case:locations.studios.art.props.1.label": "Studio B",
 "case:locations.studios.art.props.2.label": "Control room",
 "case:locations.studios.art.props.3.label": "Rack wall",
 "case:locations.studios.art.props.4.label": "Glass",
 "case:locations.studios.description": "The studios are two dark, padded rooms joined by a glass-fronted control room. Studio A has the microphone used by Tom Hargreaves. Studio B is smaller and usually used for interviews. Marcus’s body was found there beside a low tape machine and a brass reel weight.",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_automation.label": "The broadcast rack",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_automation.text": "The automation rack is still warm. Its screen shows the overnight schedule, a list of audio files, and an option called Auto-Rescue. A green dot says the stream never lost connection.",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_b.label": "Studio B",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_b.text": "Studio B has been photographed but not cleaned. Marcus lies beside the table, one hand under his jacket. The door was not forced. On the table, a brass reel weight sits just outside the dark outline where it had been moved.",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_listener.label": "The listener recording",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_listener.text": "A listener has sent the station a recording from Friday night. At 23:07, beneath Tom’s voice, there is a tiny repeating click. It is the same click heard on an earlier test file in the automation rack.",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_ticket.label": "The maintenance queue",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_ticket.text": "Ben Bell’s maintenance queue is open on the control-room terminal. One ticket records a fault in the rack’s Auto-Rescue input, closed at 18:42. A second note says the system was left in fallback mode for the night.",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_tom.label": "Tom’s microphone",
 "case:locations.studios.hotspots.hs_studio_tom.text": "Tom’s microphone is live, but the chair is pushed back and a paper cup has gone cold. The clock in Studio A is five minutes slow. On the desk is a receipt from the pub across the quay, time-stamped during the part of the programme Tom says he was speaking live.",
 "case:locations.studios.name": "The studios",
 "case:locations.studios.summary": "Studio A, Studio B, the control room, and the racks that keep Rookery on air.",
 "case:setting": "North Quay · Brighton · October 2026",
 "case:sketchCredit": "SKETCH: FRIDAY 16 OCTOBER 2026 · NOT TO SCALE",
 "case:sketchTitle": "ROOKERY AUDIO",
 "case:stayLabel": "Stay at Rookery Audio",
 "case:tagline": "A voice on air, a deal at midnight, and a door left open.",
 "case:timeline.conclusion": "At 20:35 Tom argued with Marcus about the sale. Anika left at 21:07, and Iris’s last archive scan was at 21:41. Marcus was killed in Studio B at about 22:18 and found at 22:30. The late-night programme began at 23:00, after the murder, even though Tom’s voice was already in the system.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_anika.teaser": "Something the road remembers.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_anika.text": "Anika leaves in a taxi",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_argument.text": "Tom argues with Marcus about the sale",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_argument.time": "20:35",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_death.text": "Marcus is killed in Studio B",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_death.time": "22:18",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_found.text": "Ben finds Marcus and calls the police",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_found.time": "22:30",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_scan.teaser": "A machine remembers a hand.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_scan.text": "Iris’s last archive scan is recorded",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_show.text": "The late-night programme begins",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_show.time": "23:00",
 "case:timeline.prompt": "Put the events in the order they really happened. Times you know for certain are shown; reason out the rest.",
 "case:timeline.title": "Friday night, reconstructed",
 "case:title": "The Last Track",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_ben_auto.insight": "Ben’s own maintenance ticket says the fallback would play the scheduled file and warns staff not to call it live. The automation log shows exactly that happened.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_ben_auto.response.0": "I read the warning. I wrote the warning.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_ben_auto.response.1": "I thought Tom would be in Studio A before the fallback reached the microphone. When he wasn’t, the rack did what I had told it to do.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_ben_auto.response.2": "I was embarrassed. I didn’t think a bad handover made me part of a murder.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_ben_auto.response.3": "Ben hid what he knew about the false broadcast, but the records still put him on the equipment side of the night, not on the archive route.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_ben_auto.title": "The warning on the ticket",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_felix_approval.insight": "The sale memo says the announcement depends on Marcus’s approval, and his messages show he intended to stop it until Clearwater was resolved.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_felix_approval.response.0": "…Marcus had not signed. Not finally.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_felix_approval.response.1": "I thought the pressure of a midnight announcement would bring him round. That is how acquisitions work: deadlines make decisions visible.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_felix_approval.response.2": "I was trying to close a deal, not prevent him from speaking. If I had wanted the announcement without him, I would not have left the building.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_felix_approval.response.3": "Felix was willing to push Marcus past his own deadline. The pressure is real, but the hotel record still places Felix away from the murder window.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_felix_approval.title": "Not yet approved",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_archive.insight": "Iris’s last scan was at 21:41. The archive door opened again at 22:12, during the exact period when the corridor camera has no view.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_archive.response.0": "The scanner records the file, not every minute I spent in the building.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_archive.response.1": "I went to the reception desk to look for the missing schedule. Then I heard something from the studios and checked the corridor. That is all.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_archive.response.2": "Her careful alibi has a gap: she was not continuously in the archive, and the unseen passage opens during the death window.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_archive.title": "The archive did not hold her",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_clearwater.insight": "Clearwater’s 17 percent fee is amended to pay IC Consulting Ltd, whose director and signatory is Iris Chen.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_clearwater.response.0": "…You found the photocopy.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_clearwater.response.1": "IC Consulting was a way to be paid for work Marcus refused to recognise. I built the rights schedule, negotiated the licences, and kept Rookery’s catalogue alive while he chased the sale.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_clearwater.response.2": "It was not theft. It was an arrangement. Marcus could have disclosed it and paid me properly. Instead he was going to make it look like a trapdoor under the deal.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_clearwater.response.3": "Iris admits the private financial interest Marcus had threatened to expose.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_clearwater.title": "Not an ordinary vendor",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_key.insight": "Master B opened Studio B’s rear panel at 22:13. The key was signed out to Iris and never returned.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_key.response.0": "I did not use it on Studio B.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_key.response.1": "The rear panel opened with keyed access at 22:13 and closed at 22:20. The public door was untouched until after that.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_key.response.2": "…Then someone took it from the archive door. I do not know who.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_key.response.3": "Iris’s key statement no longer fits the door record. The unseen route was used by the person who held Master B.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_iris_key.title": "Master B went farther",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_tom_live.insight": "The first forty-five minutes of the programme came from a fallback file. Tom was at the Anchor Tap when the voice on air greeted the listeners.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_tom_live.response.0": "…The opening was recorded. Yes.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_tom_live.response.1": "Ben told me the rack was temperamental, and I thought I could get a drink before the live link. The fallback was supposed to be a safety net, not a lie.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_tom_live.response.2": "I was angry at Marcus. I was not in the building when he was killed. If you’re looking for the person who used the recording, look at who knew the system would do it.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_tom_live.response.3": "Tom’s live alibi collapses, but the recording also places him away from Studio B during the murder window.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_tom_live.title": "A voice without a room",
 "deductions:deductions.d_broadcast.conclusion": "The 23:00 voice was a recording. Auto-Rescue played Tom’s fallback file for forty-five minutes, so the sound of Tom on air cannot place Tom inside Studio A. The programme began after Marcus died, and the system was capable of making a missing person sound present.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_broadcast.options.0": "Tom was physically live in Studio A",
 "deductions:deductions.d_broadcast.options.1": "A recorded fallback was playing while Tom was elsewhere",
 "deductions:deductions.d_broadcast.options.2": "The station’s stream had failed completely",
 "deductions:deductions.d_broadcast.options.3": "Marcus had taken over Tom’s programme",
 "deductions:deductions.d_broadcast.proofLabels.0": "What the rack played",
 "deductions:deductions.d_broadcast.proofLabels.1": "What the listener heard",
 "deductions:deductions.d_broadcast.question": "What does the 23:00 broadcast prove?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_broadcast.title": "The voice on air",
 "deductions:deductions.d_deal.conclusion": "Marcus had found a continuing 17 percent claim on Rookery’s archive income. The Clearwater agreement redirected that money to IC Consulting, and the arrangement had to be disclosed before Vesper could safely buy the company.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_deal.options.0": "A routine invoice for Vesper’s public announcement",
 "deductions:deductions.d_deal.options.1": "A private agreement diverting archive income through Clearwater Rights",
 "deductions:deductions.d_deal.options.2": "A failed microphone repair charged to Ben",
 "deductions:deductions.d_deal.options.3": "A second offer to buy Rookery from Felix",
 "deductions:deductions.d_deal.proofLabels.0": "The ledger entry",
 "deductions:deductions.d_deal.proofLabels.1": "The agreement behind it",
 "deductions:deductions.d_deal.question": "What had Marcus found in the archive?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_deal.title": "The missing percentage",
 "deductions:deductions.d_last.conclusion": "Marcus died between 22:10 and 22:25. Studio B’s rear panel opened at 22:13 and closed at 22:20, while the public door stayed untouched. Someone used the hidden route during the murder window.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_last.options.0": "The public door opened at 22:22",
 "deductions:deductions.d_last.options.1": "The rear panel opened at 22:13 and closed at 22:20",
 "deductions:deductions.d_last.options.2": "Ben ran into the building at 22:29",
 "deductions:deductions.d_last.options.3": "The radio programme began at 23:00",
 "deductions:deductions.d_last.proofLabels.0": "When Marcus died",
 "deductions:deductions.d_last.proofLabels.1": "The keyed door record",
 "deductions:deductions.d_last.question": "What places someone in Studio B during the death window?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_last.title": "The rear door",
 "deductions:deductions.d_route.conclusion": "The archive passage runs behind the acoustic wall and opens directly onto Studio B’s rear service panel. It is outside the camera’s view, and Master B opens both ends.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_route.options.0": "By leaving through the loading-yard door",
 "deductions:deductions.d_route.options.1": "Through the archive passage with Master B",
 "deductions:deductions.d_route.options.2": "By hiding inside Studio A until the camera reset",
 "deductions:deductions.d_route.options.3": "By entering through the river windows",
 "deductions:deductions.d_route.proofLabels.0": "The building route",
 "deductions:deductions.d_route.proofLabels.1": "The access and blind spot",
 "deductions:deductions.d_route.question": "How could someone reach Studio B without appearing in the public corridor?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_route.title": "Behind the soundproofing",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.conclusion": "Iris controlled the rights agreement that Marcus was about to expose, and she held the Master B key used on the archive-to-Studio B route. Her last archive scan and the rear-panel opening occupy the same missing stretch of the night.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.options.0": "Tom Hargreaves",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.options.1": "Iris Chen",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.options.2": "Anika Rao",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.options.3": "Felix Ward",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.proofLabels.0": "Who controlled the private agreement",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.proofLabels.1": "Who held the route’s key",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.question": "Who connects the hidden deal to the hidden route?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_who.title": "The person with both keys",
 "dialogues:statements.st_anika_left.text": "I left Rookery just after nine and did not come back.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_anika_marcus.text": "Marcus delayed the sale because he found a clause he did not like.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_ben_auto.text": "I didn’t realise Auto-Rescue could make Tom sound live without a live check.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_ben_control.text": "I was in the control room until I found Marcus at 22:30.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_felix_deal.text": "The sale required a clean archive with no undisclosed claim on its income.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_felix_left.text": "I left Rookery before nine and went straight to my hotel.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_iris_archive.text": "I stayed in the archive from after the Vesper meeting until Ben shouted from Studio B.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_iris_clearwater.text": "Clearwater Rights was a routine catalogue administration arrangement, not my private account.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_iris_key.text": "I left Master B in the archive door and never used it on Studio B.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_tom_argument.text": "I told Marcus he could sell the building, but he could not sell my voice.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_tom_live.text": "I was live in Studio A when Rookery After Dark began at 23:00.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_departure.lines.0": "Anika, when did you leave Rookery?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_departure.lines.1": "Just after nine. Marcus told me the announcement might be delayed, and I had a train to catch. I locked the staff door behind me.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_departure.lines.2": "I was at the station before half past nine. I did not come back, and I did not know Marcus was dead until Clare called.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_departure.lines.3": "If you want to check, check the door and the taxi. I am tired of being the responsible person who looks guilty because she keeps the receipts.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_departure.prompt": "When did you leave?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_sale.lines.0": "Why was Marcus suddenly talking about stopping the sale?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_sale.lines.1": "Because he found a clause he didn’t like. Marcus could turn one bad line in a contract into a personal insult.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_sale.lines.2": "I told him to send it to the lawyers. He said the lawyers had been sent everything except the truth. That was Marcus: a sentence, a storm, and no paperwork.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_sale.lines.3": "I needed the sale to close. So did he. Rookery has been living from invoice to invoice for a year.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_anika_sale.prompt": "Why was Marcus delaying the sale?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_fallback.lines.0": "Why was Auto-Rescue armed for Tom’s show?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_fallback.lines.1": "It had a fault. I repaired the input but didn’t trust it until I could replace the card on Monday.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_fallback.lines.2": "Fallback is normal. It plays a recorded opening if the microphone drops. I didn’t realise it would run the whole opening without a live check.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_fallback.lines.3": "I should have put a warning on the schedule. I did put one on the ticket. That is the kind of mistake that gets you fired, not arrested.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_fallback.prompt": "Why was the fallback running?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_night.lines.0": "Ben, what were you doing when Marcus was killed?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_night.lines.1": "In the control room, mostly. I was checking the rack and waiting to see if the fallback would behave. At 22:30 I went to Studio B and found him.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_night.lines.2": "I called the police from reception. I didn’t move anything except the door, because I thought the room needed air.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_night.lines.3": "The camera will show me running in. It won’t show what happened before that. Nobody was in the corridor when I checked the monitor.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_ben_night.prompt": "What were you doing at 22:30?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_sale.lines.0": "What did Clause 7.3 require before Vesper could buy Rookery?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_sale.lines.1": "A clean archive. No undisclosed claims on the catalogue income. Standard acquisition language.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_sale.lines.2": "Marcus had accepted the clean-archive clause. If he had a problem with an outside arrangement, he should have raised it in the data room. Vesper does not kill sellers; we walk away from them.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_sale.lines.3": "I wanted the announcement at midnight because the market wanted it. That is pressure, not a murder weapon.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_sale.prompt": "What was in the sale agreement?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_visit.lines.0": "Felix, when did you leave your meeting with Marcus?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_visit.lines.1": "At twenty to nine. We had agreed the announcement would go ahead. Marcus was difficult, but he had not walked away from eighteen million pounds.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_visit.lines.2": "I went straight to the Brighton Marine. I had a room booked there and a call with London at ten.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_visit.lines.3": "I never saw Marcus after I left the warehouse. If he changed his mind, he did it after I was gone.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_felix_visit.prompt": "When did you leave Rookery?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_archive.lines.0": "Iris, where were you after Felix left?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_archive.lines.1": "In the archive. Marcus wanted the rights schedule checked before the announcement, and I was the person who could do it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_archive.lines.2": "I stayed there until I heard Ben shout from Studio B. I did not go into either studio. The archive has enough work in it without borrowing somebody else’s crisis.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_archive.lines.3": "The scanner records my work. So does the door. If you want an alibi, start with the machines.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_archive.prompt": "Where were you after the Vesper meeting?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_key.lines.0": "The register says you signed out Master B. Where is it now?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_key.lines.1": "In the archive door, I thought. I was carrying a stack of files and must have left it there when I went back to the desk.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_key.lines.2": "I did not use it on Studio B. I have no reason to enter a recording room during a rights audit.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_key.lines.3": "Marcus was alive the last time I saw him. He was angry about the sale, but he was not in danger from me.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_key.prompt": "What happened to Master B?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_rights.lines.0": "The ledger has Clearwater Rights taking seventeen percent of the archive income. What was that?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_rights.lines.1": "A catalogue administration arrangement. Rookery is a small company; we outsource specialist work when we need it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_rights.lines.2": "The Vesper team had the schedule. Marcus knew the arrangement existed. It was not a secret, and it was not my private account.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_rights.lines.3": "I spent Friday making sure the archive was ready for disclosure. That is what the rights department does.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_iris_rights.prompt": "Tell me about Clearwater Rights.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_marcus.lines.0": "What did you and Marcus argue about at 20:35?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_marcus.lines.1": "My contract. Vesper wanted to fold the show into a national network and call it a cost saving. Marcus said he’d protect my slot. He said a lot of things.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_marcus.lines.2": "I told him he could sell the building, but he couldn’t sell my voice. It sounded good in the moment. It sounds awful now.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_marcus.lines.3": "Then I left him to meet Felix and went across the quay. I did not touch Marcus.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_marcus.prompt": "What did you argue about?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_show.lines.0": "Tom, where were you when Rookery After Dark began?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_show.lines.1": "In Studio A, where I always am. I did the opening live, took a caller, and settled into the show.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_show.lines.2": "Marcus had just spent an hour telling me the sale would make me replaceable. I went on air and did my job. That is the part of the night I can prove.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_show.lines.3": "You heard me, didn’t you? The whole quay did.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_tom_show.prompt": "Where were you when your programme began?",
 "evidence:evidence.anika_taxi.detail": "Receipt from Brighton Cars.\n\nPickup: Rookery Audio, North Quay\nBooked: 21:04\nPaid: 21:12\nDestination: Hove station\nCardholder: A. Rao\n\nThe driver’s initials are written in the margin. The company confirms the car was dispatched from the quay and dropped its passenger at Hove station at 21:27.",
 "evidence:evidence.anika_taxi.name": "Anika’s taxi receipt",
 "evidence:evidence.anika_taxi.summary": "Anika Rao paid for a taxi from North Quay at 21:12, matching her claim that she left before the murder.",
 "evidence:evidence.archive_scan_log.detail": "Local activity report from the archive scanner and door contact.\n\n21:32:17 · staff code IC-04 · Clearwater folder opened\n21:41:03 · staff code IC-04 · page 2 scanned\n21:41:08 · staff code IC-04 · archive door closed\n22:12:54 · archive door opened · key contact\n22:20:48 · archive door closed\n\nThe scanner has no scan between 21:41 and Monday. The door-contact report uses the same Master B key family as the Studio B rear panel.",
 "evidence:evidence.archive_scan_log.name": "The archive scan log",
 "evidence:evidence.archive_scan_log.summary": "Iris’s staff code made the last archive scan at 21:41, and the archive door opened again at 22:12 without a new scan.",
 "evidence:evidence.automation_log.detail": "Export from Rookery’s broadcast automation rack.\n\n18:42:11 · B. Bell · Auto-Rescue input fault closed\n18:42:19 · THL_2300_FALLBACK.wav loaded for 23:00\n22:58:00 · scheduled programme armed\n23:00:00 · THL_2300_FALLBACK.wav started\n23:00–23:45 · microphone input: none\n23:45:00 · station ident inserted\n23:47:02 · live input resumed\n\nThe file is a complete recording of Tom Hargreaves’s usual opening monologue. Auto-Rescue is designed to make a recorded host sound live when the studio feed fails.",
 "evidence:evidence.automation_log.name": "The automation log",
 "evidence:evidence.automation_log.summary": "At 23:00 the station played THL_2300_FALLBACK.wav automatically. No microphone input was logged during the first forty-five minutes.",
 "evidence:evidence.ben_ticket.detail": "Maintenance ticket BB-441, opened at 18:16 and closed at 18:42.\n\nFault: Auto-Rescue input intermittently drops the live microphone.\nAction: reseated the input card, tested with a rehearsal file, left fallback mode enabled until Monday.\nEngineer: Ben Bell.\n\nBen has initialled the warning: ‘If live feed fails after 23:00, the system will play the scheduled fallback. Do not call it live.’",
 "evidence:evidence.ben_ticket.name": "Ben’s maintenance ticket",
 "evidence:evidence.ben_ticket.summary": "Ben Bell repaired the Auto-Rescue input at 18:42 and left the fallback file armed for the night shift.",
 "evidence:evidence.broadcast_schedule.detail": "Rookery After Dark, Friday 16 October.\n\n23:00–01:00 · Host: Tom Hargreaves · Studio A · live link required\n23:00 fallback · THL_2300_FALLBACK.wav · loaded by B. Bell at 18:42\n23:45 station ident\n00:00 Vesper Media acquisition announcement, subject to Marcus Vale’s approval\n\nThe schedule is printed in Iris Chen’s handwriting, with one note in Marcus’s red pen: ‘No announcement until I sign the archive schedule.’",
 "evidence:evidence.broadcast_schedule.name": "The broadcast schedule",
 "evidence:evidence.broadcast_schedule.summary": "Tom Hargreaves’s programme was scheduled for 23:00, with a fallback file already loaded into the automation system.",
 "evidence:evidence.clearwater_contract.detail": "Photocopy of the two-page Clearwater Rights agreement, dated 3 March 2025.\n\nRookery Audio grants Clearwater Rights a continuing 17 percent administration fee on selected archive licences. The handwritten amendment on page two instructs Clearwater to pay the fee to IC Consulting Ltd ‘as management consideration’.\n\nCompany number 11820471 belongs to IC Consulting Ltd. The director listed at Companies House is Iris Chen. Iris’s signature appears beside the amendment, although the original page is missing from the archive box.\n\nMarcus’s red pen circles the words ‘continuing’ and ‘before completion’.",
 "evidence:evidence.clearwater_contract.name": "The Clearwater agreement",
 "evidence:evidence.clearwater_contract.summary": "The private agreement routes archive money to IC Consulting, a company controlled by Iris Chen.",
 "evidence:evidence.corridor_camera.detail": "Recovered clips from the camera above reception.\n\n22:09:44 · Anika Rao crosses from the staff entrance toward reception.\n22:11:03 · the public corridor is empty; Studio A’s red light is on.\n22:11:04–22:21:18 · no clip available. The camera reports an alarm-state interruption.\n22:21:19 · the corridor is empty again.\n22:22:06 · Studio B’s public door opens from the inside and closes after three seconds.\n22:29:17 · Ben Bell runs into view from reception.\n\nThe camera cannot see the archive passage or Studio B’s rear service panel.",
 "evidence:evidence.corridor_camera.name": "The corridor camera",
 "evidence:evidence.corridor_camera.summary": "The camera shows the public corridor empty at 22:11, then loses its clips until 22:21. Studio B’s public door opens at 22:22.",
 "evidence:evidence.entry_log.detail": "Building access report for Friday.\n\n20:01 · staff entrance opened by Iris Chen\n20:04 · public entrance opened by Felix Ward\n20:48 · public entrance closed by Felix Ward\n21:07 · staff entrance opened by Anika Rao\n21:08 · staff entrance closed by Anika Rao\n22:29 · public entrance opened by Ben Bell\n\nNo other exterior door events are recorded between 21:08 and 22:29. The loading-yard alarm remained set.",
 "evidence:evidence.entry_log.name": "The entry log",
 "evidence:evidence.entry_log.summary": "The public entrance stayed locked after 20:48; the loading-yard door was armed all night.",
 "evidence:evidence.felix_hotel.detail": "The Brighton Marine’s night report, printed at 23:02.\n\nGuest: Felix Ward\nReservation: Vesper Media\nCheck-in: 21:36\nRoom key issued: 21:37\nLift key used: 21:39\nRoom 508 door opened: 21:40\n\nThe hotel is a twelve-minute drive from North Quay in Friday traffic. Felix’s coat was damp when he arrived, and the receptionist remembers him asking for a glass of water.",
 "evidence:evidence.felix_hotel.name": "Felix’s hotel record",
 "evidence:evidence.felix_hotel.summary": "Felix Ward checked into the Brighton Marine at 21:36, with a key-card use at 21:39.",
 "evidence:evidence.key_register.detail": "The sign-out sheet clipped beneath the reception key cabinet.\n\nMaster A · 17:55 · B. Bell · rack inspection · returned 18:42\nMaster B · 20:02 · I. Chen · archive audit · not returned\n\nAt the bottom, in Clare’s handwriting: ‘Iris says she left it in the archive door. Police did not find it there.’ The Master B key opens the archive’s staff door and the rear service panel in Studio B.",
 "evidence:evidence.key_register.name": "The master-key register",
 "evidence:evidence.key_register.summary": "Master B was signed out by Iris Chen at 20:02 for an archive audit and was not returned before the police arrived.",
 "evidence:evidence.listener_recording.detail": "Audio file sent to Rookery at 23:18 by listener Priya Nair.\n\nAt 23:07 Tom appears to say: ‘If you’re awake, you’re in the right place.’ Behind the words is a short chair squeak followed by two breaths. The same chair squeak and the same two breaths occur at 23:08 in the reference recording made during Thursday’s rehearsal.\n\nPriya writes: ‘I thought the show sounded unusually polished. I was listening from my flat in Kemptown.’",
 "evidence:evidence.listener_recording.name": "The listener’s recording",
 "evidence:evidence.listener_recording.summary": "A listener’s phone recording captures the same breath and chair squeak twice, proving the 23:07 link was a replay.",
 "evidence:evidence.marcus_messages.detail": "Messages between Marcus and his sister Clare on Friday.\n\n19:48 Marcus: Found a payment trail in the archive that doesn’t belong in the Vesper pack.\n19:49 Clare: You’re selling the company in three hours. What does ‘doesn’t belong’ mean?\n19:51 Marcus: It means somebody has been taking a percentage of our old catalogue before it reaches the company account.\n19:55 Clare: Who?\n19:57 Marcus: I’m checking the signature. Don’t call anyone yet.\n20:02 Marcus: If the Clearwater page is what I think it is, I’m stopping the announcement.\n20:04 Clare: Marcus.\n20:05 Marcus: I know. I’ll tell you when I know.\n\nThere are no later messages.",
 "evidence:evidence.marcus_messages.name": "Marcus’s messages",
 "evidence:evidence.marcus_messages.summary": "Marcus told Clare he had found a private rights arrangement inside Rookery’s archive and might stop the sale.",
 "evidence:evidence.passage_note.detail": "The passage behind the acoustic wall is less than a metre wide. Dust on the floor is broken only at the archive door and the rear panel. A crescent of fresh blue-grey paint has transferred from the archive door to the latch plate.\n\nThe red door-contact light is visible from neither studio. The passage contains no microphone, camera, or motion sensor. Anyone using it would reach Studio B without appearing in the public corridor.",
 "evidence:evidence.passage_note.name": "The staff passage",
 "evidence:evidence.passage_note.summary": "Blue-grey paint is fresh on the passage latch, and the route has no camera or sound pickup.",
 "evidence:evidence.police_summary.detail": "Preliminary notes made by Detective Sergeant Leah Morley at 23:15 on Friday.\n\nMarcus Vale, 51, founder and CEO of Rookery Audio. Found by Benjamin Bell in Studio B at 22:30. Death appears to have occurred between 22:10 and 22:25, pending the pathologist’s examination.\n\nOne blunt-force injury to the left side of the head. A brass tape-reel weight was found on the floor near the body. No sign of forced entry. Wallet, phone and watch remain on the victim.\n\nThe front door was locked from the inside. The staff entrance alarm was set. The central corridor camera has a gap in its clips between 22:11 and 22:21. The archive passage is not covered by any camera.\n\nThe sale of Rookery Audio to Vesper Media was due to be announced at midnight. All staff who were present have been asked to remain available.",
 "evidence:evidence.police_summary.name": "The police summary",
 "evidence:evidence.police_summary.summary": "Marcus Vale was killed in Studio B between 22:10 and 22:25 and found at 22:30. A brass reel weight may be the weapon.",
 "evidence:evidence.rights_ledger.detail": "Rookery Audio rights ledger, current through September 2026.\n\nMost archive licences are paid directly to Rookery Audio Ltd. One line is different:\n\nCLEARWATER RIGHTS · catalogue administration · 17% of gross licence income · schedule pending\n\nThe beneficiary column has been covered with correction fluid. In the margin Marcus has written: ‘Who approved this? Check against Vesper 7.3.’ The entry is initialled I.C.",
 "evidence:evidence.rights_ledger.name": "The rights ledger",
 "evidence:evidence.rights_ledger.summary": "A pencil entry sends 17 percent of Rookery’s archive licensing income through Clearwater Rights before Vesper sees it.",
 "evidence:evidence.sale_memo.detail": "Confidential heads of terms between Rookery Audio Ltd and Vesper Media Group, 9 October 2026.\n\nPurchase price: £18,000,000, subject to completion accounts and transfer of the Rookery Audio archive.\n\nClause 7.3: The seller warrants that no third party has a continuing right to a percentage of licensing income from the catalogue except those listed in Schedule C.\n\nSchedule C is marked ‘to follow’. In the margin beside Clause 7.3 Marcus has written: ‘Do not sign until Clearwater is resolved.’",
 "evidence:evidence.sale_memo.name": "The Vesper sale memo",
 "evidence:evidence.sale_memo.summary": "Vesper’s offer depends on receiving Rookery’s archive rights cleanly. Marcus marked one clause for review.",
 "evidence:evidence.station_layout.detail": "Rookery Audio’s original warehouse plan, annotated after the studios were soundproofed.\n\nThe public corridor runs from reception past Studio A to Studio B. Behind the acoustic wall is a staff passage connecting the archive to Studio B’s rear service panel. The passage is not visible from reception and has no camera.\n\nThe archive door and Studio B’s rear panel both accept Master B. The plan notes that the passage should remain locked, but the archive’s door-contact light is the only alarm.",
 "evidence:evidence.station_layout.name": "The warehouse plan",
 "evidence:evidence.station_layout.summary": "The archive’s staff door opens onto a narrow passage that reaches the back of Studio B without crossing reception.",
 "evidence:evidence.studio_b_panel.detail": "Door-contact report from Studio B.\n\n22:13:08 · rear service panel opened · keyed access\n22:20:41 · rear service panel closed\n22:22:06 · public door opened from inside\n22:22:09 · public door closed\n\nThe rear panel opens directly onto the archive passage. On the inside frame is a small smear of blue-grey paint, the colour used on the archive door. The brass reel weight was on the floor by the mixing desk; the table has one fresh crescent-shaped dent.",
 "evidence:evidence.studio_b_panel.name": "Studio B’s rear panel",
 "evidence:evidence.studio_b_panel.summary": "The rear service panel opened at 22:13 with a key and closed at 22:20. The public door was untouched until 22:22.",
 "evidence:evidence.tom_receipt.detail": "Card receipt from the Anchor Tap, across the quay.\n\nFriday 16 October · 23:06:14\n1 × tonic water · £2.80\nCard ending 0419 · T. Hargreaves\n\nThe bartender remembers Tom sitting in the window alcove from shortly after eleven until the station ident at 23:45. Tom’s phone connected to the pub’s Wi-Fi at 23:05.",
 "evidence:evidence.tom_receipt.name": "Tom’s pub receipt",
 "evidence:evidence.tom_receipt.summary": "Tom paid for a drink at the Anchor Tap at 23:06, during the programme’s first recorded link.",
 "evidence:evidence.visitor_log.detail": "Friday’s visitor page.\n\n20:04 · Felix Ward · Vesper Media · meeting Marcus Vale · signature\n20:48 · Felix Ward · departure · signature\n\nThe next line is blank. The ink on Felix’s departure signature is still slightly shiny, as if the book was closed soon after. A second paper cup has left a ring beside the page, but there is no name beside it.",
 "evidence:evidence.visitor_log.name": "The visitor book",
 "evidence:evidence.visitor_log.summary": "Felix Ward signed in at 20:04 and out at 20:48. Anika’s name is absent, despite a second cup at the desk.",
 "suspects:suspects.anika.bio": "Anika co-founded Rookery with Marcus and has spent the last year trying to make its finances orderly enough to sell. She is direct, tired, and protective of the staff. She says she left before nine to take a train home after Marcus told her the sale might be delayed.",
 "suspects:suspects.anika.dismissal": "You’re building a theory out of an unpleasant meeting.",
 "suspects:suspects.anika.name": "Anika Rao",
 "suspects:suspects.anika.rebuttal": "I was the person trying to keep Rookery alive. Marcus could be impossible, but I had no reason to silence him.",
 "suspects:suspects.anika.role": "The chief operating officer",
 "suspects:suspects.ben.bio": "Ben keeps the studios, racks, and cables alive. He is good with equipment and bad with explanations, especially after a shortcut goes wrong. He found Marcus at 22:30 and admits he knew the late-night show could fall back to a recording.",
 "suspects:suspects.ben.dismissal": "That’s not how the rack works. Or the night. Or any of this.",
 "suspects:suspects.ben.name": "Ben Bell",
 "suspects:suspects.ben.rebuttal": "I left the system in fallback because I was fixing it. I found Marcus, called the police, and stayed here. That’s everything.",
 "suspects:suspects.ben.role": "The sound engineer",
 "suspects:suspects.felix.bio": "Felix Ward negotiated Vesper Media’s eighteen-million-pound offer. He is polished, impatient, and accustomed to people calling a deadline a crisis. He met Marcus at Rookery at 20:04 and says he left with the deal intact.",
 "suspects:suspects.felix.dismissal": "You’re confusing leverage with motive.",
 "suspects:suspects.felix.name": "Felix Ward",
 "suspects:suspects.felix.rebuttal": "I had a commercial disagreement with Marcus. Killing him would destroy the transaction I was paid to close.",
 "suspects:suspects.felix.role": "The Vesper acquisition lead",
 "suspects:suspects.iris.bio": "Rookery’s head of rights, and the person who can name almost every voice in its archive. Iris joined Marcus three years ago after working for a major catalogue company. She speaks carefully, keeps the archive immaculate, and says the Vesper sale is the only way Rookery can survive.",
 "suspects:suspects.iris.dismissal": "I’m afraid you’ve mistaken a routine rights audit for a crime.",
 "suspects:suspects.iris.name": "Iris Chen",
 "suspects:suspects.iris.rebuttal": "I managed those rights because somebody had to. Marcus made promises to everyone and kept records for no one. I did not kill him.",
 "suspects:suspects.iris.role": "The head of rights",
 "suspects:suspects.tom.bio": "The voice of Rookery After Dark: quick, funny, and more popular than the station that employs him. Tom had a loud argument with Marcus about the Vesper sale earlier in the evening. At 23:00, his programme sounded as if he were still in Studio A.",
 "suspects:suspects.tom.dismissal": "That’s a very dramatic way to misunderstand radio.",
 "suspects:suspects.tom.name": "Tom Hargreaves",
 "suspects:suspects.tom.rebuttal": "Marcus and I fought about a contract. I was angry, not murderous. And if you want to know where I was, ask the pub.",
 "suspects:suspects.tom.role": "The late-night host"
}
